# The dev server's log. `npm run dev` must be started detached with its output
# redirected to a file — an attached stdout that stops being read kills Next on
# an uncaught EPIPE, and the process then spins instead of exiting while every
# request hangs. See CLAUDE.md.
dev.log

# 🔓 Real Venmo statements. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC, and a downloaded
# statement carries real payer names, real transaction IDs and real amounts for
# people who never agreed to be in a git history — a third party's name in a
# public repo is not something a later commit can take back.
#
# Keep them locally, never commit one. The fabricated example that IS committed
# is docs/VenmoStatement_August_2026.csv, built entirely from seed members; it
# is what any parser or import work should be developed against.
docs/VenmoStatement_*.csv
!docs/VenmoStatement_August_2026.csv

# UI design skills are COMMITTED as of 2026-09-18 (DESIGN.md §Design toolkit), so
# every clone carries the same pinned toolkit. Licences, and the one skill whose
# upstream publishes no LICENSE file: .claude/third-party-licenses/README.md.
# settings.local.json stays machine-local; the shared hooks are in settings.json.
.claude/settings.local.json
__pycache__/

# Playwright's run output (npm run test:ui).
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/

# 📌 DESIGN.md, PRODUCT.md and .impeccable/design.json are NOT ignored, and that
# is deliberate (2026-08-17). They are Impeccable OUTPUT rather than vendored
# tooling: DESIGN.md is the design source of truth for the whole site, PRODUCT.md
# records the product context and the refusals (no photography, no invented
# statistics), and design.json is the machine sidecar `/impeccable doctor` diffs
# for staleness. Leaving them untracked meant the binding spec existed on one
# laptop. `.impeccable/config.json` is tracked for the same reason: its detector
# ignores are DESIGN DECISIONS with their evidence attached (the hero's 60×60
# grid is the handoff's spec, not generated-UI decoration), and left untracked
# the next officer's hook re-raises every one of them. Everything else
# Impeccable writes under .impeccable/ is session state:
.impeccable/*
!.impeccable/design.json
!.impeccable/config.json
# The detector findings accepted as standing (tests/design-detector.test.ts).
# Untracked, every clone would scan against an empty file it never received.
!.impeccable/baseline.json
# Surface briefs (DESIGN.md §Design toolkit, step 1). They are impeccable's
# own briefs so the lead skill loads them, and they are binding design records:
# the brief guard hook and the receipts test both read them.
!.impeccable/surfaces/

# Real photographs of members. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#
# 🔓 **`public/photos/` IS NOW COMMITTED — officer decision, 2026-08-19.** The
# officer was asked directly, with the tradeoff stated, and chose to publish so
# the rest of the committee could review the redesign on the live site. What
# they signed off on: 126 web-sized images, 9 of them referenced by `src` in
# `lib/site.ts` and 117 forming the home marquee's pool.
#
# ⚠️ **This is the irreversible half, and it stays written down.** A third
# party's FACE in a public git history is not something a later commit takes
# back — `git rm` removes it from the tip and leaves it in every clone and in
# every previous commit. Undoing this means rewriting history and
# force-pushing, and it still does not reach forks or caches. Every one of these
# is an identifiable student. **If a member asks to be removed, that is a
# history rewrite, not a delete — plan for it accordingly.**
#
# 📌 `pictures/` stays ignored and is NOT part of that decision. It is the
# officer's raw local library (originals, HEIC, unsorted), it is much larger,
# and nothing serves from it — `scripts/build-photos.mjs` derives
# `public/photos/` from it.
#
# 📌 A file under `public/` is fetchable at its own URL whether or not any page
# links it. That is why the original `public/photos/` was DELETED rather than
# unlinked in 2024-08-14, and it is why adding a photo here publishes it even
# if no slot points at it yet.
pictures/

# Personal, non-project files that happen to sit in this working directory.
# The repository is PUBLIC and history is not takeable-back, so keep them out
# of reach of a broad `git add -A`. Better still, keep them outside the repo.
Claude outputs/
